### Sample requests (IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client)
### Full cinema flow. Run the requests from top to bottom; ids assume an empty database.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8090

### Login as the bootstrap admin -> copy accessToken into @adminToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "admin@tickets.local", "password": "Admin@12345"}

###
@adminToken = paste-admin-token-here

### Admin: create a movie
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/movies
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Angkor Legends",
  "description": "An adventure among the temples of Angkor",
  "durationMinutes": 120,
  "ageRating": "G"
}

### Admin: create an R18 movie
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/movies
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Night in Phnom Penh", "durationMinutes": 105, "ageRating": "R18"}

### Public: list movies
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/movies

### Admin: create a hall (rows A-E STANDARD, F VIP, G COUPLE = 50 seats)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/halls
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Koh Pich Hall",
  "rows": [
    {"row": "A", "seats": 8, "type": "STANDARD"},
    {"row": "B", "seats": 8, "type": "STANDARD"},
    {"row": "C", "seats": 8, "type": "STANDARD"},
    {"row": "D", "seats": 8, "type": "STANDARD"},
    {"row": "E", "seats": 8, "type": "STANDARD"},
    {"row": "F", "seats": 6, "type": "VIP"},
    {"row": "G", "seats": 4, "type": "COUPLE"}
  ]
}

### Public: one hall with its seats
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/halls/1

### Admin: schedule a showtime (7 PM Phnom Penh time; VIP = 1.5 x, COUPLE = 2 x basePrice)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/showtimes
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"movieId": 1, "hallId": 1, "startsAt": "2030-04-14T12:00:00Z", "basePrice": 4.00}

### Public: upcoming showtimes (optionally for one movie)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/showtimes?movieId=1

### Public: seat map with prices and availability
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/showtimes/1/seats

### Register a customer (dateOfBirth is optional, but needed for PG13 / R18 movies) -> copy accessToken into @token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "dara@example.com", "password": "Password123", "fullName": "Sok Dara", "dateOfBirth": "1998-03-21"}

###
@token = paste-customer-token-here

### Who am I
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Hold seats for 10 minutes (any client-side price is ignored; retrying with the same Idempotency-Key returns the same booking)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: dara-a3-a4-f1

{"showtimeId": 1, "seats": ["A3", "A4", "F1"]}

### Pay for the held seats -> copy ticketCode into @ticketCode
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/1/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
@ticketCode = paste-ticket-code-here

### My bookings
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One booking
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin: check the ticket in at the door (opens 1 hour before the start)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketCode}}/check-in
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Cancel a booking (customers can't cancel a paid booking within 2 hours of the start)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin: change the price of a showtime (movie, hall and start time are fixed once seats are sold)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/showtimes/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"movieId": 1, "hallId": 1, "startsAt": "2030-04-14T12:00:00Z", "basePrice": 4.50}

### Admin: cancel a showtime (also cancels all its held and paid bookings)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/showtimes/1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
